## Technologies Used

- **Spring Boot** (REST API, dependency injection, caching)
- **Spring Data JPA** (ORM and repository pattern)
- **MySQL** (Relational database)
- **Redis** (Caching layer)
- **Lombok** (Boilerplate reduction)
- **Maven** (Build and dependency management)
- **Postman** (API testing)

## Installation and Setup

### Prerequisites

- JDK 11 or later
- Maven
- MySQL server (create a database named `ems_db`)
- Redis server (or use Docker for Redis)

### Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/employee-management-system.git
cd employee-management-system
```

### Configure the Application

Edit `src/main/resources/application.properties` with your database and Redis credentials:

```properties
# MySQL Configuration
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/ems_db?useSSL=false&serverTimezone=UTC
spring.datasource.username=root
spring.datasource.password=your_password

spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
spring.jpa.show-sql=true

# Redis Configuration
spring.redis.host=127.0.0.1
spring.redis.port=6379
```

## Running the Application

### Using Maven

```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```

### Using the Packaged Jar

```bash
mvn clean package
java -jar target/employee-management-system.jar
```

The application will start on port `8080`.

## API Endpoints

### Employees

- **GET /api/employees**
  _Description_: Retrieve all employees.
  _Example Response_:
  ```json
  [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "john.doe@example.com",
      "role": "Developer",
      "department": "IT",
      "employer": {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "Tech Corp",
        "address": "123 Main St"
      },
      "skills": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "skillName": "Java"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "skillName": "Spring Boot"
        }
      ],
      "projects": [
        {
          "id": 3,
          "projectName": "Project Alpha",
          "description": "Alpha description"
        }
      ],
      "skillIds": [1, 2],
      "projectIds": [3]
    }
  ]
  ```

- **GET /api/employees/{id}**
  _Description_: Retrieve an employee by ID.

- **POST /api/employees**
  _Description_: Create a new employee.
  _Example Request Body_:
  ```json
  {
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "role": "Developer",
    "department": "IT",
    "skillIds": [1, 2],
    "projectIds": [3, 4]
  }
  ```

- **PUT /api/employees/{id}**
  _Description_: Update an existing employee.
  _Example Request Body_:
  ```json
  {
    "name": "John Doe Updated",
    "email": "john.doe@example.com",
    "role": "Senior Developer",
    "department": "IT",
    "skillIds": [1, 2, 5],
    "projectIds": [3, 4, 6]
  }
  ```

- **DELETE /api/employees/{id}**
  _Description_: Delete an employee.

### Employers, Skills, and Projects

Similar endpoints are available for employers (`/api/employers`), skills (`/api/skills`), and projects (`/api/projects`). Refer to the controller files for details.

